addresses.comment:
**`ai = yes`: nobody is playing the scope's country.** 0x5ED3B0 to the single `ret 4` at 0x5ED477, 6 int3 after. The game state is fetched get-or-create (the inlined `new(0xDA8)` block), then

    return (state->played_countries_array (+0xBCC) [scope->country_id (+0x14)] == 0) == this->value (+0x40)

+0xBCC is used as a **pointer** to one dword per country id. `ai = no` is a real test (a played country). Country 0 is not tested for; it reads entry 0.

**`casus_belli = TAG`: the scope's country could go to war on TAG with some casus belli now.** 0x5E7C60 to the single `ret 4` at 0x5E7CE1.

    other = this->target (+0x40/+0x44)
    if (arg_is_this (+0x18)) other = scope->this_scope (+0x38) ->country (+0x10/+0x14)
    elif (arg_is_from (+0x19)) other = scope->this_scope ->from_country (+0x18/+0x1C)
    return DiplomacyStatus_HasUsableCasusBelli(us->diplomacy (+0xE28) [other.id], &scope->country_tag, &other)   // 0x649CA0

THIS is read straight off this_scope, **without** EventScope_GetCountryTag's fall-back to the province owner - unlike guarantee, military_access, non_aggression_pact, truce_with, undeclared_war_with, vassal_of and war_with. For what counts as usable see 0x649CA0/0x649D80.

**`has_strategic_resource`: the scope's province has a real strategic resource - and the value is never read.** 0x604F90 to the single `ret 4` at 0x605048.

    return state->provinces_begin (+0xB8C) [scope->province (+0x28)] ->strategic_resource (+0x18) ->slot14()

Slot 14 is ReturnTrue on CStrategicResource and ReturnFalse on CNullStrategicResource. `this` is not read, so **`has_strategic_resource = no` answers exactly as `= yes`**. No test for province 0 or a null resource pointer; RebuildStrategicResourceProvinces (0x28BB90) dispatches the same slot unguarded over every province from index 0, so the pointer is never null in practice.
